; Phase E e4f: blocking pthread_cond_wait. Earlier 1 ms timedwait_relative_np was a missed-signal
; band-aid that, under macOS arm64 with 3+ concurrent supervised actors, drove a libpthread
; internal kwq malloc storm racing with new-actor TLS instantiation (mfm_alloc
; KERN_PROTECTION_FAILURE SIGBUS in _calloc / _tlv_get_addr). All wake paths for the call
; wrapper (worker reply, supervisor cascade kill+restart, etc.) hold wrapper#72 and signal
; wrapper#24 before unlock, so a properly-locked plain wait is sufficient. We still check
; reply_set on each wake to absorb spurious wakeups.
